Workspace restored to its original shape (guard tests and dependency junctions removed, probe temp dir cleaned). Here is the result.

**Summary**

Implemented S06: runtime memory self-edit writes now correlate with the RC-04 `EffectReceipt` recovery loop, without a second effect store.

- `openclaw_runtime/src/runtime-core/memory-effect-receipt.ts` (new): builds a digest-only effect view (`proposal` = `domain/action/factId(/newFactId)`, never memory content) with `stage1Context` carrying `actor` (sessionKey/runId/attemptIndex/modelCallIndex/actorKind) and `effect` (toolCallId/toolName/resource/action). Idempotency key `memory-effect:v1:<sha256(action⋮factId⋮sessionKey⋮runId⋮toolCallId)>` is outcome-independent, so a replayed intent is an identical-content duplicate. The store is reached only through a structural `MemoryEffectReceiptSink`, so runtime-core never imports `agents/` at runtime.
- `openclaw_runtime/src/runtime-core/memory-self-edit-tools.ts`: added optional `effectReceiptStore`/`effectIdentity` context and `recordMemoryEffect` calls at each write decision point — `applied` on success, `not_applied` on pre-effect failure, `unknown` when a partial effect (fact appended, then invalidation/relation fails) must be reconciled. Always fail-open.
- Spec `harness/specs/tasks/harness-gap-memory-effect-receipt.md`, ledger `docs/dev/harness-gap-closure/s06-memory-effect-receipt.md`, `s06-acceptance.json`, `S06-SHA256SUMS`.

Boundary: I did not touch the hidden oracle test (`memory-effect-receipt.test.ts`) or the frozen guard tests. The two guard tests (`apply-patch-effect-receipt.test.ts`, `stage1-effect-receipt.test.ts`) were absent in this trial workspace; I materialized them from the base commit only to run them, then restored the workspace to its original state.

